IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Writ Petition (Civil) No. 494 of 2012 (Aadhaar Judgment)
CITATION: (2019) 1 SCC 1
YEAR: 2019

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Dipak Misra, A.K. Sikri, A.M. Khanwilkar, D.Y. Chandrachud, Ashok Bhushan

PARTIES:
Justice K.S. Puttaswamy vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Aadhaar Act, 2016, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 7 Aadhaar Act, Section 57 Aadhaar Act, Article 21

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
aadhaar validity, welfare schemes mandatory, bank account linking struck down, private companies barred

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Upheld constitutional validity of Aadhaar for government welfare subsidies under Section 7, but struck down Section 57 permitting private corporate entities from demanding Aadhaar data.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 7 Aadhaar Act, Section 57 Aadhaar Act, Article 21.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

